Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 20:17:29 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] Where does the salinity drift? Model against GLORYS monthly
 means, maps and regions

analysis/salinity_drift.jl compares the run's monthly means (from the daily
output) with GLORYS's monthly means (GLORYSMonthly), both on the model grid:
maps of model - GLORYS surface salinity and top-200 m salinity and
temperature, per month and at the start (initial state against GLORYS's
first day, as a check); by region (Beaufort Gyre, central Arctic, Siberian
shelves, Barents Sea, Nordic Seas, Archipelago, Baffin Bay) the mean
differences and the liquid freshwater content relative to 34.8; and the
model's daily freshwater content through the run. Tables in
output_dir/salinity_drift.md, figures salinity_drift_maps.png and
salinity_drift_fwc.png.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
